{
  "title": "Stage 2: Averages and letters",
  "summary": "GroupBy each student, Average their scores and map them to letters with a switch expression.",
  "minutes": 14,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: one average per student",
      "body": [
        "A list of scores is not a gradebook yet. A teacher wants one line per student: their average and a letter.",
        "",
        "That is a **grouping** question. `GroupBy` collects the items that share a key into groups; each group has a `Key` and is itself a sequence you can run more LINQ on:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "var averages = scores",
        "    .GroupBy(s => s.Student)                  // one group per student",
        "    .Select(g => new",
        "    {",
        "        Student = g.Key,",
        "        Average = g.Average(s => s.Points)    // LINQ inside the group",
        "    })",
        "    .OrderBy(a => a.Student)",
        "    .ToList();",
        "```",
        "",
        "The letter comes from a **switch expression** with relational patterns. Arms are tried top to bottom and the first match wins:",
        "",
        "```csharp",
        "string Letter(double average) => average switch",
        "{",
        "    >= 90 => \"A\",",
        "    >= 80 => \"B\",",
        "    >= 70 => \"C\",",
        "    >= 60 => \"D\",",
        "    _ => \"F\"",
        "};",
        "```",
        "",
        "From this stage on the program stops listing every score and prints the counts line followed by the summaries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "Groups are sequences too. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "var scores = new[] { (\"Ada\", 90), (\"Ben\", 70), (\"Ada\", 80), (\"Ben\", 75), (\"Cy\", 60) };",
        "",
        "foreach (var g in scores.GroupBy(s => s.Item1))",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{g.Key} {g.Count()} {g.Average(s => s.Item2)}\");"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "Ada 2 85",
        "Ben 2 72.5",
        "Cy 1 60"
      ],
      "explain": "Groups come out in the order each key was first seen: Ada, Ben, Cy. Ada's average is (90 + 80) / 2 = 85, Ben's is 72.5."
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "A colleague wrote the arms in this order. What letter does an average of `95` get?",
      "code": [
        "string Letter(double average) => average switch",
        "{",
        "    >= 60 => \"D\",",
        "    >= 70 => \"C\",",
        "    >= 80 => \"B\",",
        "    >= 90 => \"A\",",
        "    _ => \"F\"",
        "};"
      ],
      "options": [
        "`D`",
        "`A`",
        "`C`",
        "It does not compile"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "Arms are checked top to bottom and `95 >= 60` is true, so the first arm wins. Put the most specific test first. (The compiler only complains when an arm can *never* be reached; here every arm can be.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Arrange the query that prints each student's average, alphabetically.",
      "lines": [
        "var averages = scores",
        "    .GroupBy(s => s.Student)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Student = g.Key, Average = g.Average(s => s.Points) })",
        "    .OrderBy(a => a.Student)",
        "    .ToList();"
      ],
      "explain": "Group first, so there is a `Key` to read and a group to average; then sort the summaries; `ToList()` ends the query."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Averages and letter grades",
      "carry": true,
      "prompt": [
        "Replace the list of scores with a summary per student.",
        "",
        "1. Stop printing each score. Keep the `Scores: N, skipped: M` line.",
        "2. Print an empty line, then `Averages:`.",
        "3. Group the scores by student, average each group, sort by name, and print `Name: average letter` with the average to one decimal place.",
        "4. Write `string Letter(double average)` as a switch expression: 90 and up `A`, 80 `B`, 70 `C`, 60 `D`, below 60 `F`.",
        "",
        "For this input:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "student,course,score",
        "Ada,Math,91",
        "Ada,Physics,78",
        "Ada,History,84",
        "Ben,Math,85",
        "Ben,Physics,64",
        "Ben,History,70",
        "Cy,Math,88",
        "Cy,Physics,92",
        "Dee,Math,88",
        "Dee,Physics,55",
        "Dee,History,97",
        "Eve,Math,59",
        "Eve,History,84",
        "Eve,Physics,oops",
        "```",
        "",
        "print exactly:",
        "",
        "```text",
        "Scores: 13, skipped: 1",
        "",
        "Averages:",
        "Ada: 84.3 B",
        "Ben: 73.0 C",
        "Cy: 90.0 A",
        "Dee: 80.0 B",
        "Eve: 71.5 C",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var rows = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var scores = rows",
        "    .Select(TryParseScore)",
        "    .OfType<Score>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "foreach (var s in scores)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{s.Student} | {s.Course} | {s.Points}\");",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}, skipped: {rows.Count - scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "Score? TryParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;",
        "    if (points < 0 || points > 100) return null;",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), points);",
        "}",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "var lines = new List<string>();",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) is not null)",
        "    lines.Add(line);",
        "",
        "var rows = lines",
        "    .Where(l => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(l))",
        "    .Where(l => !l.StartsWith(\"student,\"))",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "var scores = rows",
        "    .Select(TryParseScore)",
        "    .OfType<Score>()",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine($\"Scores: {scores.Count}, skipped: {rows.Count - scores.Count}\");",
        "",
        "var averages = scores",
        "    .GroupBy(s => s.Student)",
        "    .Select(g => new { Student = g.Key, Average = g.Average(s => s.Points) })",
        "    .OrderBy(a => a.Student)",
        "    .ToList();",
        "",
        "Console.WriteLine();",
        "Console.WriteLine(\"Averages:\");",
        "foreach (var a in averages)",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"{a.Student}: {a.Average:F1} {Letter(a.Average)}\");",
        "",
        "Score? TryParseScore(string line)",
        "{",
        "    var parts = line.Split(',');",
        "    if (parts.Length != 3) return null;",
        "    if (!int.TryParse(parts[2], out var points)) return null;",
        "    if (points < 0 || points > 100) return null;",
        "    return new Score(parts[0].Trim(), parts[1].Trim(), points);",
        "}",
        "",
        "string Letter(double average) => average switch",
        "{",
        "    >= 90 => \"A\",",
        "    >= 80 => \"B\",",
        "    >= 70 => \"C\",",
        "    >= 60 => \"D\",",
        "    _ => \"F\"",
        "};",
        "",
        "record Score(string Student, string Course, int Points);"
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "a class of five",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score",
            "Ada,Math,91",
            "Ada,Physics,78",
            "Ada,History,84",
            "Ben,Math,85",
            "Ben,Physics,64",
            "Ben,History,70",
            "Cy,Math,88",
            "Cy,Physics,92",
            "Dee,Math,88",
            "Dee,Physics,55",
            "Dee,History,97",
            "Eve,Math,59",
            "Eve,History,84",
            "Eve,Physics,oops"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Scores: 13, skipped: 1",
            "",
            "Averages:",
            "Ada: 84.3 B",
            "Ben: 73.0 C",
            "Cy: 90.0 A",
            "Dee: 80.0 B",
            "Eve: 71.5 C"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "the messy input from stage 1",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score",
            "Ada,Math,91",
            "Ben,Math,abc",
            "Ada,Physics,78",
            "",
            "Cy,Math,88",
            "Dee,Math,101",
            "Ben,Physics,64",
            "Eve,Math",
            "Cy,Physics,88",
            "Dee,Physics,55"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Scores: 6, skipped: 3",
            "",
            "Averages:",
            "Ada: 84.5 B",
            "Ben: 64.0 D",
            "Cy: 88.0 B",
            "Dee: 55.0 F"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a tiny class",
          "stdin": [
            "Zed,Chemistry,72",
            "Amy,Chemistry,95",
            "Amy,Biology,81",
            "Zed,Biology,58",
            "Kim,Chemistry,72",
            "Kim,Biology,",
            "Kim,Biology,90"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Scores: 6, skipped: 1",
            "",
            "Averages:",
            "Amy: 88.0 B",
            "Kim: 81.0 B",
            "Zed: 65.0 D"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "no scores",
          "stdin": [
            "student,course,score"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "Scores: 0, skipped: 0",
            "",
            "Averages:"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "require": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\.GroupBy\\(",
          "message": "Groups with GroupBy"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\\.Average\\(",
          "message": "Uses Average"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "switch\\s*\\{",
          "message": "Uses a switch expression"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`scores.GroupBy(s => s.Student).Select(g => new { Student = g.Key, Average = g.Average(s => s.Points) })`",
        "Sort with `.OrderBy(a => a.Student)`. Format with `{a.Average:F1}`.",
        "`string Letter(double average) => average switch { >= 90 => \"A\", >= 80 => \"B\", >= 70 => \"C\", >= 60 => \"D\", _ => \"F\" };`"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
